Changes made in this port, as required by section 4(b) of the license:

  - The lid angle sensor reader was removed. Mac Duo reads an Apple
    `AppleSPUHIDDevice` (HID usage page 0x20, usage 0x8A) that reports the hinge
    angle directly. No equivalent exists on a normal Windows laptop, so the angle
    is instead produced by a scripted sweep in
    `src/main/defaults.js` and smoothed by the same critically damped spring.
  - Screen capture was reimplemented on Electron's `desktopCapturer` in place of
    ScreenCaptureKit.
  - Metal and MetalPerformanceShaders were replaced by WebGL2, and the Gaussian
    pyramid by mip levels sampled through `textureLod`.
  - The Metal fragment shader's dimming, which raises its factor to 2.2 because
    the original samples an sRGB texture and works in linear light, becomes a
    direct multiply because this port never decodes the texture.
  - The AppKit overlay window, menu bar item and SwiftUI settings panel were
    replaced by an Electron BrowserWindow, a tray menu, and an HTML settings
    page.
  - The lid angle sensor and its whole trigger policy (velocity prediction,
    pre-warm capture, hysteresis, idle timeout) were removed along with it, and
    replaced by a global hotkey and a tray menu item.

Files that carry ported logic, with their Mac Duo counterparts:

  src/renderer/lib/geometry.js   <-> Sources/MacDuo/DepthOverlay.swift
  src/renderer/lib/homography.js <-> Sources/MacDuo/Homography.swift
  src/renderer/lib/shader.js     <-> Sources/MacDuo/DepthShaders.swift
  src/renderer/lib/spring.js     <-> Sources/MacDuo/CriticallyDampedSpring.swift
  src/renderer/lib/gradient.js   <-> Sources/MacDuo/BlurGradient.swift
  src/main/defaults.js           <-> Sources/MacDuo/Preferences.swift
